    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a two-stage points \u2192 level system.\n\n**Points (`MembershipPoints.of`, new class):** start at 0; +2 email present; +1 `namesakeCount` is 0; +2 household of 3 or more (`householdSize >= 3`); +3 tenure over 365 days.\n\n**Level (`MembershipLevel.of`, rewritten):** now derives from points via `fromPoints` \u2014 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\n**Wiring:**\n- `OwnerMapper` now maps both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel`.\n- `openapi.yml` gains the `membershipPoints` field and the `membershipLevel` description/constraints were updated (max raised from 3 to 4, since the old \"level 4 reserved for tenure / capped at 3\" scheme is gone). Since the DTOs are generated from the spec, this also produces the new `membershipPoints` getter/setter.\n\nThe acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest`) \u2014 a fresh owner with an email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 3 points / level 2 \u2014 passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
