    "probe_text": "I now have the full pipeline. Here is the complete, ordered list of what happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n**Authorization** \u2014 the endpoint file requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`; without that role the request is denied (handled by the `AuthorizationDeniedException` escalation).\n\nEvery step below runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all reads and the final write share one transaction that commits once at the end.\n\n## Pipeline order\n\n**1. `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 validation + normalization (the only step that reads the body)**\nReads `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` once and republishes it. Collects *all* errors, then throws `OwnerFieldsInvalidException` (400) if any exist:\n- Required, must be non-blank: `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`.\n- **Address** (required): normalized via `AddressNormalizer` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). If blank after normalization \u2192 `\"address\"` error; otherwise the canonical form is written back onto the request.\n- **Telephone**: normalized to E.164 via `TelephoneE164` (strip spaces/dashes/brackets; assume `+61` and drop a leading `0` when no `+`; enforce 8\u201315 total digits, and exact national length for `+61`=9 / `+1`=10). Invalid \u2192 `\"telephone\"` error; valid \u2192 written back.\n- **Email** (optional): if present, must match the email regex and its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Invalid/disposable \u2192 `\"email\"` error; valid \u2192 stored trimmed + lower-cased.\n- **Postcode** (optional): if present, must be a 4-digit value valid for the `city` per `Postcode.isValidForCity` (a city with no known region accepts any 4-digit code). Invalid \u2192 `\"postcode\"` error; valid \u2192 stored trimmed.\n- **RegistrationDate** (optional): if present, must not be after today; a future date \u2192 `\"registrationDate\"` error.\n\nNote: `@RequestBody` here is *not* `@Valid`, so bean-validation constraints on the DTO are not triggered \u2014 validation is exactly the checks above.\n\n**2. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed); if \u2265 50 \u2192 `OwnerCityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n**3. `CheckOwnerDailyLimit`** \u2014 computes the effective registration date (supplied or today), rolls it to a business day (`BusinessDay.adjust`, weekend \u2192 Monday), counts existing owners registered on that business day; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `OwnerDailyLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n**4. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`; defaults `registrationDate` to today if absent, then rolls it forward to a business day and stores the adjusted date.\n\n**5. `AssignHousehold`** \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalize(lastName) + \"|\" + postcode`. Deterministic; same last name + postcode \u21d2 same household.\n\n**6. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`** \u2014 if any existing owner shares this `householdId` \u2192 `OwnerIdentityConflictException` (409), **unless** the request set `sharesHousehold=true`, which bypasses the check.\n\n**7. `AssignHouseholdSize`** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = count of existing owners sharing the `householdId`, plus 1 for this owner (1 if `householdId` is null).\n\n**8. `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, where REGION is `Locality.regionOf(postcode)` and HASH8 is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n\n**9. `AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first + last name (case-insensitive), excluding this one.\n\n**10. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if more than 80 owners already exist for this owner's registration business day, else false.\n\n**11. `AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 soft-match flag. If `sharesHousehold=true`, sets `possibleDuplicate=false`/`possibleDuplicateOf=null`. Otherwise, if an existing owner (non-null postcode) shares this owner's `postcode` + `lastName` (case-insensitive) but has a *different* telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = that owner's id (lowest id if several match); else false/null.\n\n**12. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 persists the owner via `ownerRepository.save` (generates the id).\n\n**13. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 logs an audit line on the `AUDIT` logger with id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and computed `MembershipLevel`.\n\n**14. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n### Summary of the two categories\n\n- **Validations (can reject before persisting):** required fields, address/telephone/email/postcode/registration-date validity (400); city capacity \u226550 (409); daily limit \u2265100 (429); household-identity uniqueness (409).\n- **Side-effects applied to the entity/system:** field normalization (address, telephone, email, postcode) written back; registration date defaulted + business-day-adjusted; and the derived fields `householdId`, `householdSize`, `customerCode`, `namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`; then persistence, an audit log line, and the 201 response \u2014 all committed in one transaction."
